# Line-ending policy (2026-10-21).
#
# The repo has NO .gitattributes, and this host's git has core.autocrlf=true.
# That combination silently converted shell scripts to CRLF in the working
# tree, which produced a shebang of `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` — and the script
# then failed with:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# The health watchdog (scripts/vishwas_health_probe.sh) is executed directly
# by cron, so a CRLF shebang makes it fail 100% of the time — and the failure
# is silent from the operator's point of view (cron just logs a line).
#
# Pin the policy per file type so it cannot depend on the developer's local
# autocrlf setting.

# Shell scripts MUST be LF: their shebang is interpreted by the kernel.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Python is safe either way, but LF is canonical for a Linux deployment.
*.py    text eol=lf

# Config/env files consumed by systemd EnvironmentFile.
*.env   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Documentation and prose: keep the author's choice.
*.md    text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.wav   binary
*.pth   binary
*.safetensors binary
*.onnx  binary
*.pem   text eol=lf
